# GitHub Private Preflight (Template)

Copy this file to `github-private-preflight.mdc` locally and fill in your private values.

```bash
cd /path/to/repo && \
git config --local core.sshCommand 'ssh -i ~/.ssh/<your_private_key> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes' && \
git remote set-url origin git@<your-github-host-alias>:<your-org-or-user>/<your-repo>.git && \
mkdir -p ~/.config/<your-gh-profile> && \
GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/<your-gh-profile> gh auth status && \
git config --local --get core.sshCommand && \
git remote -v
```

If GH auth is missing:

```bash
GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/<your-gh-profile> gh auth login -h github.com -p https -w
```
